<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">1992 Summer Olympics</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Barcelona 1992</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1992 Summer Olympics were held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, from 25 July to 9 August 1992. The first Games after the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> without a major boycott, they included a Unified Team of former Soviet republics and a reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> returned after decades of exclusion. The preparations transformed the city's waterfront and transport, and became a model for urban renewal through the Olympics.</p></div>
